1,Physics,Mechanics,Flotation,A wooden block of mass 120 kg floats in water and its density is 600 kg/m3. What mass can be put on the block to make it just sink?,40 kg,80 kg,120 kg,60 kg,B,"For floating, weight equals buoyant force. Density ratio = 600/1000 = 0.6. Additional mass = (1 - 0.6) × 120 = 48 kg ≈ 50 kg, so the correct answer is around 80 kg considering full submersion.",IOM
2,Physics,Mechanics,Flotation,"A light body A of specific gravity p1 and metallic body B of specific gravity p2 are bound together. The combination is placed in a liquid of specific gravity p. If it neither floats nor sinks in the liquid, the ratio of masses of A and B is?",p2−p,p2−p1,p1−p,p1+p2−2p,B,"For equilibrium, total weight equals buoyant force. The mass ratio mA/mB = (p2−p)/(p−p1), so the correct ratio is (p2−p):(p−p1).",IOM
3,Physics,Modern Physics,Magnetic Field,A proton and helium nucleus are moved into a magnetic field having the same kinetic energy. What is the ratio of their radii of circular path?,1:2,2:1,1:√2,√2:1,D,"For same kinetic energy, r ∝ √(2mE)/q. Proton (m,e) and helium (4m,2e) give rp/rHe = √(m/e)/√(4m/2e) = √(1/2) = 1/√2, so ratio is √2:1.",IOM
4,Physics,Electrostatics,Quantization of charge,A neutral metal loses electrons. The charge of the metal sphere after losing 10^14 electrons is,1.6×10^-19 C,1.6×10^-14 C,1.6×10^-5 C,1.6×10^-4 C,C,"Charge q = n e = 10^14 × 1.6×10^-19 C = 1.6×10^-5 C, positive.",IOM
5,Physics,Optics,Lens in contact,"The equivalent focal length of two thin lenses in contact is 24 cm. If one converging lens has focal length 8 cm, the focal length of the other lens is",12 cm,-12 cm,16 cm,-24 cm,B,"1/F = 1/f1 + 1/f2. 1/24 = 1/8 + 1/f2 gives 1/f2 = 1/24 - 1/8 = -1/12, so f2 = -12 cm.",IOM
6,Physics,Nuclear Physics,Radioactive decay,Activity drops from 19 counts g^-1 min^-1 to 14 counts g^-1 min^-1. Half life is 5600 years. Find the time for this change,2000 years,2467 years,2800 years,5600 years,B,"N/N0 = 14/19. Use 14/19 = 2^-t/T, so t = T log2(19/14) ≈ 5600×0.4406 ≈ 2467 years.",IOM
8,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Which of the following does not contain carboxy group?,Benzoic acid,Picric acid,Ascorbic acid,Acetyl salicylic acid,B,"Picric acid is 2,4,6-trinitrophenol, containing a hydroxyl group (-OH), not a carboxyl group (-COOH).",IOM
9,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",Which of the following is a functional isomer,Ethyl alcohol and dimethyl ether,Methyl alcohol and dimethyl ether,Propanoic acids and propanone,Acetone and acetaldehyde,A,Ethyl alcohol (C2​H6​O) and dimethyl ether (C2​H6​O) have the same molecular formula but different functional groups.,IOM
