32,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The molality of 15% (w/v)  of a solution of H2​SO4​ (density=1.1 g/cc) is,1.7 m,1.5 m,1.6 m,1.8 m,A,Calculation: Mass of solution in 1 L=1100 g. Mass H2​SO4​=150 g. Mass of solvent =1100−150=950 g. Moles H2​SO4​=150/98≈1.53 mol. Molality=1.53 mol/0.95 kg≈1.6 m. (Answer A or C is likely correct depending on rounding/option error). Using C: 1.6 m.,IOM
