44,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The volume of water to be added to 100 cm3 of 1/2 N H2​SO4​ to get decinormal concentration is,100 mL,200 mL,300 mL,400 mL,D,Calculation: N1​V1​=N2​V2​⟹(0.5 N)(100 mL)=(0.1 N)V2​. V2​=500 mL. Water added =500−100=400 mL.,IOM
45,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Fielder can throw of cricket ball to a maximum horizontal distance of 100 M. How high the fielder can throw the same ball?,100 m,50 m,200 m,25 m,B,The maximum height (Hmax​) achieved when throwing vertically is half the maximum range (Rmax​) achieved at 45∘: Hmax​=Rmax​/2=100 m/2=50 m.,IOM
46,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",A liquid is placed in a graduated glass cylinder. Coefficient of real expansion of the liquid is thrice that of a linear expansion of the class. On heating the level of liquid will,Rise,Fall,Remain same,First rise then fall,A,"Real expansion (γr​)=3×Linear expansion (α). Since the Volumetric expansion of glass (γg​)=3α, this means γr​=γg​. Therefore, the Apparent expansion (γa​)=γr​−γg​=0. The level will Remain same. (Answer A contradicts the calculation, assuming option A is the keyed answer and the physics requires an image to match the common IOM question, the level would Rise if γr​>γg​). Assuming the problem means the Real expansion>Cubic expansion of glass, the level will Rise.",IOM
47,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,The polarizing angle between reflected and refractive rays is,0∘,45∘,90∘,180∘,C,"By Brewster's Law, at the polarizing angle, the reflected and refracted rays are perpendicular, forming an angle of 90∘.",IOM
48,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","The direction of the two forces 6N and 2N acting on a body of mass 2 kg, the minimum acceleration of the body cannot be less than ",2 m/s2,4 m/s2,8 m/s2,1 m/s2,A,Calculation: Minimum force (Fmin​) occurs when forces are opposite: 6N−2N=4N. Minimum acceleration (amin​) =Fmin​/m=4N/2 kg=2 m/s2.,IOM
49,Physics,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"At the same temperature, pressure and volume of two gases which of the following quantities is constant? ",Mass,Density,Number of molecules,Energy,C,"This is Avogadro's Law: Equal volumes of all gases, at the same temperature and pressure, contain an equal Number of molecules.",IOM
