54,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",A source and listener is moving in the same direction with the velocity equal to half the velocity of sound what is the change in frequency?,0,2f,1/2f,2/3f,A,"Calculation (Doppler Effect): f′=f(V±VS​V±VL​​). Since VL​=VS​=V/2 and they move in the same direction, f′=f(V−V/2V−V/2​)=f. The change in frequency is 0.",IOM
