65,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",An aeroplane moving with 300 km/hr in circular path then what is change in velocity in half revolution?,300 km/hr,600 km/hr,0,150 km/hr,B,"Calculation: In half a revolution, the final velocity vector is opposite the initial one. Change in velocity Δv=vf​−vi​=(−v)−(v)=−2v. The magnitude is 2v=2×300=600 km/hr.",IOM
66,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,A body cover 1/3rd distance with v1​ velocity next 2/3rd distance with v2​ velocity then average velocity,v1​+2v2​3v1​v2​​,2v1​+v2​3v1​v2​​,v1​+v2​v1​v2​​,2v1​+v2​​,B,"Calculation: t1​=(D/3)/v1​=D/(3v1​), t2​=(2D/3)/v2​=2D/(3v2​). Vavg​=t1​+t2​D​=D/(3v1​)+2D/(3v2​)D​=v2​+2v1​3v1​v2​​.",IOM
67,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,Heater is 1000W then energy consumed in two hours is,1000 J,2000 J,2 kWh,4000 J,C,Calculation: Energy = Power × Time =1000 W×2 hours=1 kW×2 h=2 kWh.,IOM
68,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,25W−220 V and 100W−220 V is joined in series with 220V mains then power will be,25 W,100 W,20 W,125 W,C,"Calculation: Resistance R=V2/P. R25​=2202/25, R100​=2202/100. Pseries​=V2/(R25​+R100​)=V2/(V2/25+V2/100)=1/(1/25+1/100)=1/(5/100)=20 W.",IOM
