74,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Heat is flowing through two cylinder of same material.  The diameter for rods are in ratio. 1:2 and their length is 2:1. If the temperature difference between their end are same the ratio amount of heat inducted through them per unit time will be,1:8,8:1,1:2,4:1,A,"Calculation: Heat flow H∝LA​∝LD2​. D1​/D2​=1/2, L1​/L2​=2/1. H1​/H2​=D22​/L2​D12​/L1​​=(D2​D1​​)2×(L1​L2​​)=(1/2)2×(1/2)=1/8. Ratio is 1:8.",IOM
