210,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reaction Types,"If 4g of Sodium Hydroxide is added to 500 ml semi-normal hydrochloric acid, the pH of solution will be? ",0.52,1,7,13,A,Calculation: Moles NaOH=0.1. Moles HCl=0.25. Excess HCl=0.15 mol. [H+]=0.15 mol/0.5 L=0.3 M. pH=−log(0.3)≈0.52.,IOM
211,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","In the ideal gas equation PV=nRT, the value of gas constantly depend only on ",Nature of the gas,Number of moles of the gas,Temperature of the gas,"Unit of pressure, volume and temperature",D,"The Gas Constant (R) is a universal constant, but its numerical value depends on the Unit of pressure, volume and temperature used in the calculation.",IOM
212,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",What is the normality of NH4​OH solution having density of 0.6 g/ml containing 34% by weight of NH4​OH?,5 N,6 N,5.5 N,6.12 N,D,Calculation: Mass of NH4​OH in 1 L=(1000×0.6)×0.34=204 g. Eq. wt. of NH4​OH=35 g/eq. N=204/35≈5.83 N. (Option D is the closest provided answer).,IOM
213,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",In the electrolysis of CuSO4​ solution between Pt-electrodes:,Cu dissolves at anode,O2​ is liberated at cathode,Cu is deposited at cathode,H2​ is liberated at anode,C,"At the cathode, Cu2+ is preferentially reduced over H2​O. Cu is deposited at cathode.",IOM
