216,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The reaction between phenol and CO2​ is called?,Reimer-Tiemann reaction,Friedel-Crafts reaction,Kolbe's reaction,Wurtz reaction,C,The reaction of phenol with CO2​ and base to form salicylic acid is known as Kolbe’s reaction.,IOM
217,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","If a 4g of NaOH is dissolved in water and volume is made up to 250cc, concentration in g/l will be? ",4 g/L,8 g/L,12 g/L,16 g/L,D,Calculation: Conc.=4 g/0.25 L=16 g/L.,IOM
218,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,"It is impossible to determine the position as well as momentum of an electron in an atom, this principle is known as? ",de Broglie's principle,Heisenberg's uncertainty principle,Paull's exclusion principle,Aufbau principle,B,This is the statement of the Heisenberg's uncertainty principle.,IOM
