220,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Which of the following is a reducing agent?,Cl2​,KMnO4​,H2​S,H2​SO4​,C,"Hydrogen sulfide (H2​S), where S is in its lowest oxidation state of −2, is a strong reducing agent.",IOM
221,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,Which of the following aromatic compounds is capable of hydrogen bonding?,Toluene,Phenol,Chlorobenzene,Nitrobenzene,B,Phenol (C6​H5​OH) possesses the necessary O-H group for hydrogen bonding.,IOM
