223,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"The initial volume is 400 ml and 100 degree Celsius then, find the volume at zero degree celsius ",293 mL,300 mL,312 mL,320 mL,A,Calculation (Charles's Law): V1​/T1​=V2​/T2​. V2​=V1​×T2​/T1​=400 mL×(273 K/373 K)≈292.76 mL.,IOM
224,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,Which of the compound is most reactive towards electrophile?,Benzene,Nitrobenzene,Toluene,Benzoic acid,C,Toluene is most reactive due to the +I and hyperconjugation effect of the methyl group.,IOM
225,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",In homolytic fission of hydrocarbon which is formed?,Carbocation,Carbanion,Free radical,Zwitter ion,C,"Homolytic fission (equal sharing) leads to the formation of neutral species with an unpaired electron, called Free radical.",IOM
226,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",For spontaneous reaction the value of ΔG?,Positive,Negative,Zero,None of the above,B,A spontaneous process is one that occurs with a Negative change in Gibbs Free Energy (ΔG<0).,IOM
