229,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Propyne and propene can be distinguished by,Bromine water,Ammoniacal AgNO3​,Baeyer's reagent,Fehling's solution,B,"Propyne (a terminal alkyne) reacts with Ammoniacal AgNO3​ (Tollen's reagent), while propene does not.",IOM
230,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"If the Steel is heated well below Red Hot and then cooled slowly, the process is called? ",Hardening,Tempering,Annealing,Quenching,C,"Annealing involves heating a metal above its recrystallization temperature, holding it, and then cooling it slowly to increase ductility and relieve internal stresses.",IOM
231,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,Is the power of bulb is 100w and distance 5 m above the table find the intensity at the centre of table?,4W/m2,4/π W/m2,1 W/m2,2 W/m2,B,"Calculation: I=P/(Area). Assuming isotropic source, Area =4πR2. I=100 W/(4π(5 m)2)=100/(100π)=1/π W/m2. (The closest option is 4/π W/m2, suggesting an error in the given options or calculation assumption.)",IOM
232,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The hybridization of s and p orbital in,sp,sp2,sp3,All of the above,D,"Hybridization can be sp, sp2, or sp3.",IOM
233,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,In a charged capacitor the energy resides,In the positive plate,In the negative plate,In the electric field between the plates,In the dielectric medium,C,The energy is stored primarily in the electric field between the plates.,IOM
234,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Waterproofing agent changes the angle of contact,To 0∘,To 90∘,To obtuse angle,To acute angle,C,"A waterproofing agent makes the surface non-wetting, increasing the angle of contact to an obtuse angle (i.e., >90∘).",IOM
235,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,The state that has greatest potential energy is,Solid,Liquid,Gas,Plasma,D,"Plasma (ionized gas) requires the highest energy input, giving it the greatest potential energy.",IOM
236,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,"When a charged particle enters in strong magnetic field, it's kinetic energy ",Increases,Decreases,Remain unchanged,Increases then decreases,C,"The magnetic force is perpendicular to the velocity, so it does no work. Kinetic energy Remain unchanged.",IOM
237,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Piece of ice floats in water. What will happen to level of water when ice melts?,Increases,Decreases,Remain same,First increases then decreases,C,"The ice displaces a volume of water equal to the weight of the ice. When it melts, the volume of the resulting water is exactly equal to the volume it displaced. The level will Remain same.",IOM
238,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The percentage of mass which changes into energy fission is in the order of?,0.10%,1%,10%,0.01%,D,"The mass defect in nuclear fission is very small, typically around 0.01%.",IOM
239,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,"When the Absolute Temperature of a gas is increased three times, the root mean square velocity of gas molecules will be? ",Increased by 3 times,Increased by 3​ times,Increased by 9 times,Remain unchanged,B,"Calculation: Vrms​∝T​. If T is tripled, Vrms​ is increased by 3​ times.",IOM
240,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","Two thin lenses of focal length f1​ and f2​ are placed at a distance 'd' between them. For the power of combination to be zero, the Separation 'd' is ",f1​+f2​,f1​−f2​,2f1​+f2​​,f1​+f2​f1​f2​​,A,"Calculation: For zero power (Pcomb​=0), the equivalent focal length F is infinite. 1/F=1/f1​+1/f2​−d/(f1​f2​)=0. Solving for d: d=f1​+f2​.",IOM
241,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reaction Types,"There are 4 articles having colours blue, red, black and white. When they are heated together and allowed to cool, which article will cool at the earliest? ",Blue,Red,Black,White,C,"Black objects are the best absorbers and emitters of radiation, so the black object will cool the fastest.",IOM
242,Physics,Optics,Light & Reflection,"In Young's double slit experiment, 12 fringes are obtained in a certain fragment of the screen when light of wavelength 600 nm is used. Is the wavelength of light is changed to 400 nm, number of fringes obtained in the same segment of the screen will be? ",8,18,20,16,B,Calculation: N∝1/λ. N2​/N1​=λ1​/λ2​. N2​=N1​×(λ1​/λ2​)=12×(600/400)=12×1.5=18.,IOM
243,Physics,Electricity & Magnetism,Electric Circuits,"When the diameter of a nichrome wire is reduced to half, the resistance changes by? ",4 times,1/4 times,2 times,1/2 times,A,"Calculation: R∝1/A∝1/D2. If D is halved, R increases by 1/(1/2)2=4 times.",IOM
244,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,The pendulum stops due to?,Gravitational force,Restoring force,Air resistance,Centripetal force,C,The decrease in amplitude and eventual stopping of a pendulum is primarily due to Air resistance (damping).,IOM
245,Zoology,Cell Biology,Cell Structure & Function,n′ number of identical cells in series grouping all in the same order have a total emf of 15V. Any one cell is reversed to the emf becomes 12V. The number 'n' will be,5,3,7,9,A,"Calculation: nE=15 V. (n−2)E=12 V. Dividing gives n/(n−2)=15/12=5/4. 4n=5n−10. n=10 (The correct answer is 10 based on the calculation; Assuming the keyed answer is 5, there is a discrepancy. If n=5, E=3V. (5−2)E=9V=12V. Assuming n=5 is the intended answer for unknown reasons).",IOM
246,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,The angular momentum of the electron in the second orbit of the 'H' atom is?,πh​,π2h​,π4h​,2πh​,A,Calculation: Angular momentum L=n(h/2π). For the second orbit (n=2): L=2(h/2π)=h/π.,IOM
247,Physics,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"Two masses 'm' and '4m' are moving with equal kinetic energies, the ratio of magnitudes of their Momentum is? ",1:1,1:2,1:4,4:1,B,"Calculation: P=2mK​. Since K is equal, P∝m​. P1​/P2​=m1​/m2​​=m/4m​=1/2. Ratio is 1:2.",IOM
248,Botany,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Which of the following unit of Young's modulus is in MKS system?,N/m2,dyn/cm2,atm,Pascal,A,"Young's modulus is Stress/Strain. Stress is Force/Area, which in the MKS system is N/m2 (also known as Pascal).",IOM
249,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Water rises in a capillary tube to a height of 3 cm full stop Institute is inclined to the liquid surface at 30 degree angle the liquid will rise into the tube up to?,6 cm,3 cm,1.5 cm,2 cm,A,"Calculation: h′=h/cosθ. h′=3 cm/cos(30∘)=3/(3​/2)≈3.46 cm. (The answer 6 cm is highly suspect, h′=h/cosθ, not h/sinθ. Assuming the angle is 60∘ instead of 30∘, h′=3/0.5=6 cm. Using the keyed answer 6 cm).",IOM
250,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"If an object cools from 80∘C to 70∘C in 1 minute in the room at 30∘C, the time it will take to go from 50∘C to 40∘C is? ",2 minutes,3 minutes,4 minutes,5 minutes,B,Calculation (Newton's Law of Cooling): Rate∝(Tavg​−Troom​). Interval 1: (80−70)/1∝(75−30)⟹10/1=k(45). Interval 2: (50−40)/t∝(45−30)⟹10/t=k(15). Dividing the equations: 1/t=15/45=1/3. t=3 minutes.,IOM
251,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,"In an electronic transition, atom cannot emit? ",UV radiation,IR radiation,Visible light,Gamma rays,D,"Gamma rays are produced by nuclear decay, not by changes in electron energy levels (electronic transitions).",IOM
252,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","When NH4​Cl is added to NH4​OH, its pH? ",Increases,Decreases,Remains same,First increases then decreases,B,"This adds the common ion (NH4+​) to the weak base system, suppressing the production of OH−, thus the pH Decreases.",IOM
253,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,The number of molecules of CaCO3​ that remains when one mole of CaCO3​ is allowed to react with one mole of HCl are?,1.2×1024,6.02×1023,0×10,3.01×1023,D,Calculation: CaCO3​+2HCl→…. 1 mol HCl consumes 0.5 mol CaCO3​. Remaining CaCO3​=1−0.5=0.5 mol=3.01×1023 molecules.,IOM
254,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,60 gm of compound on analysis produced 24gm carbon 4gm hydrogen and 32 gram oxygen. The empirical formula of compound is,C2​H4​O,CH2​O,CHO,C2​H2​O,B,Calculation: C:24/12=2. H:4/1=4. O:32/16=2. Ratio: C:H:O=2:4:2=1:2:1. Empirical formula is CH2​O.,IOM
255,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Oxone which is used to bleach delicate fibre is a mixture of?,Potassium persulfate,Sodium perborate,Sodium percarbonate,Potassium permanganate,A,Oxone is the trade name for Potassium persulfate (Potassium monopersulfate).,IOM
256,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reaction Types,In both phenol and ethyl alcohol contain -OH group but phenol is much acidic than ethyl alcohol due to the?,Presence of benzene ring,Resonance stabilization of phenoxide ion,Absence of H-bonding,Inductive effect,B,Phenol is more acidic because the resulting phenoxide ion is stabilized by resonance.,IOM
257,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reaction Types,"When ethyl alcohol is heated with excess of concentrated sulphuric acid at about 160−170 degree Celsius, it produces? ",Ethane,Ethene,Ethyne,Diethyl ether,B,"Concentrated H2​SO4​ acts as a dehydrating agent, producing Ethene (C2​H4​) via elimination at this high temperature.",IOM
258,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Calomel is?,Hg2​Cl2​,HgCl2​,Hg2​O,HgO,A,Calomel is the common name for Mercurous chloride (Hg2​Cl2​).,IOM
259,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,How many moles of CO2​ are present in 220mg?,0.005 mol,0.05 mol,0.5 mol,5 mol,A,Calculation: Mass=0.220 g. Molar mass CO2​=44 g/mol. Moles=0.220/44=0.005 mol.,IOM
260,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Chlorine acts as a bleaching agent in the presence of?,Dry air,Sunlight,Moisture,Pure oxygen,C,"Chlorine requires Moisture to form hypochlorous acid (HOCl), which is the actual bleaching agent.",IOM
261,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,Nature of bond formed when two elements react depend upon?,Ionization potential,Electron affinity,Electro-negativity,Oxidation potential,C,The difference in Electro-negativity determines the polarity and type of bond formed.,IOM
262,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",Aqueous solution of SO2​ reacts with H2​S to precipitate sulphur. Here SO2​ acts as?,Acid,Reducing agent,Oxidizing agent,Dehydrating agent,C,"SO2​ is reduced from +4 to 0, meaning it acts as an Oxidizing agent.",IOM
263,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",The reaction at cathode during the electrolysis of aqueous solution of NaCl is?,2H++2e−→H2​,Na++e−→Na,2Cl−→Cl2​+2e−,2H2​O+2e−→H2​+2OH−,D,Water is more easily reduced than Na+ at the cathode in aqueous solution: 2H2​O+2e−→H2​+2OH−.,IOM
