265,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Rusting of iron in moist air involves?,Loss of electrons by Fe,Oxidation of H2​O,H+ ion acts as a depolarizer,H+ ion acts as an anode,A,"Rusting is an oxidation process where Fe metal loses electrons: Fe→Fe2++2e−, which is the Loss of electrons by Fe.",IOM
266,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,CHCl3​ is stored in dark coloured bottles because,It polymerizes when exposed to sunlight,It reacts with H2​O,It gets oxidized to Phosgene gas in light,It reacts with O2​,C,"Chloroform (CHCl3​) slowly reacts with atmospheric oxygen in the presence of light to form Phosgene gas (COCl2​), a poisonous gas.",IOM
267,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Liquor poisoning is due to the presence of,Ethanol,Methanol,Propanol,Butanol,B,"Contaminated alcohol contains Methanol (wood alcohol), which is metabolized to toxic formaldehyde and formic acid.",IOM
268,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",A sample of water from a well in Terai contains 0.1gm arsenic per litre. What is the concentration of arsenic in ppm?,0.1 ppm,1 ppm,10 ppm,100 ppm,D,Calculation: 1 L of water ≈1000 g or 106 mg. Mass of As=0.1 g=100 mg. ppm=(mass of solute/mass of solution)×106=(0.1 g/1000 g)×106=100 ppm.,IOM
269,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,When two atoms of hydrogen combined to form a molecular hydrogen gas. The energy of the molecule is?,Higher than the sum of the energy of separated atoms,Lower than the sum of the energy of separated atoms,Equal to the sum of the energy of separated atoms,Infinity,B,"Bond formation is an exothermic process, so the resulting molecule has Lower than the sum of the energy of separated atoms (more stable).",IOM
270,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",Dehydration of Ethanol in excess of H2​SO4​ yields?,Ethane,Ethene,Ethyne,Diethyl ether,B,"In excess acid and high temperature (170∘C), ethanol undergoes elimination to form Ethene.",IOM
271,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,The atomic number of nitrogen is 7 and atomic number of oxygen is 8. The total number of electrons in a nitrate ion is?,30,32,31,28,B,Calculation: N(7)+3×O(8)+1 (charge)=7+24+1=32 electrons.,IOM
