278,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",A solution of sodium in liquid ammonia is blue due to the presence of?,Sodium ions,Ammoniated electrons,Sodium atoms,Sodium hydride,B,"The blue color of the dilute solution is due to the presence of Ammoniated electrons, which absorb energy in the visible region.",IOM
279,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,Which of the following electronic configuration given for some neutral atoms would be expected to have highest second ionization energy IE2​?,1s22s22p63s2 (Mg),1s22s22p63s1 (Na),1s22s22p6 (Ne),1s22s22p63s23p1 (Al),B,"Removing the first electron from Na gives Na+, which has a stable noble gas configuration (2s22p6). Removing the second electron is extremely difficult, giving it the highest IE2​.",IOM
280,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,When temperature of gas is increased its viscosity?,Increases,Decreases,Remain same,None of the above,A,"Increased temperature increases the momentum transfer between gas layers, causing the gas viscosity to Increases.",IOM
281,Physics,Optics,Light & Reflection,"The maximum wavelength emitted by the sun at the temperatures (in kelvin) T1​, T2​ and T3​ are 650 nm, 580 nm and 350 nm respectively. Which one of the following is correct? ",T1​>T2​>T3​,T1​<T2​<T3​,T1​=T2​=T3​,T1​<T3​<T2​,B,"Wien's Law: λmax​∝1/T. The smaller the wavelength, the higher the temperature. Since λ3​<λ2​<λ1​, the relationship is T1​<T2​<T3​.",IOM
282,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reaction Types,To ebonite night rods A and B of radii 1.5 cm respectively are rubbed together. Result will be?,Both become positively charged,Both become negatively charged,A becomes positively and B negatively charged,Both remain uncharged,D,Ebonite rods (hard rubber) rubbed with fur or wool would acquire a negative charge. Rubbing two identical ebonite rods together would likely result in Both remain uncharged or acquiring a very weak charge.,IOM
283,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",Power of ionization of a gamma particle is?,Very high,Very low,Same as alpha particle,None of the above,B,Gamma rays are high-energy photons with no charge. Their ability to cause ionization is Very low compared to charged particles like α or β.,IOM
284,Physics,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,The specific gravity of sugar is 1.5. Which one is the correct density in S.I. system?,1.5 kg/m3,150 kg/m3,1500 kg/m3,15000 kg/m3,C,Calculation: Density=Specific Gravity×Density of water. 1.5×1000 kg/m3=1500 kg/m3.,IOM
285,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts","If a baseball player can throw a ball to a maximum distance =d over a ground, what is the maximum vertical height to which he can throw it?  Assume that has same initial speed in each case)",d,2d,d/2,d/4,C,The maximum height (Hmax​) achieved when throwing vertically is half the maximum range (Rmax​) achieved at 45∘: Hmax​=Rmax​/2=d/2.,IOM
286,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,"When an elastic material with Young's modulus 'Y' is subjected to a stretching stress 'S', the elastic energy stored per unit volume of material is ",21​YS2,21​YS2​,S22Y​,Y2S2​,B,"Calculation: Energy density U=21​×Stress×Strain. Since Strain=Stress/Y=S/Y, U=21​×S×(S/Y)=21​YS2​.",IOM
287,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,"Two drops of water having same radius moving in air downwards with constant velocity v. If the drops ko coalesced, what will be the new velocity? ",4v,2v,22/3v,21/2v,C,"Calculation: Terminal velocity Vt​∝R2. When two drops coalesce, Rnew3​=2R3, so Rnew​=21/3R. Vnew​=Vt​×(Rnew​/R)2=Vt​×(21/3)2=22/3v.",IOM
288,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Atomic Structure,"The radius of hydrogen atom in the ground state is 0.53A.  After excitation, it is found that this radius increases to 2.12A. The value of principal quantum number will be? ",4,3,2,1,C,Calculation: rn​∝n2. n2=rn​/r1​=2.12A/0.53A=4. n=2.,IOM
289,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,What is the value of -40 degree Fahrenheit in Celsius scale?,−40∘C,−20∘C,40∘C,0∘C,A,Calculation: C=(F−32)×5/9=(−40−32)×5/9=−72×5/9=−40∘C.,IOM
290,Physics,Electricity & Magnetism,Electric Circuits,What is the potential drop across an electric hot plate which draws 5A when it is hot and resistance is 24 Ohm?,120 V,10 V,5 V,20 V,A,Calculation (Ohm's Law): V=I×R=5 A×24 Ω=120 V.,IOM
291,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,A refrigerator has to transfer an average of 263 J of heat per second from −10 degree Celsius to 25 degree Celsius. The average power consumed by the refrigerator is:,30 W,32 W,35 W,38 W,B,"Calculation: TL​=263 K, TH​=298 K. Work done (Power)=QL​/β, where β=TL​/(TH​−TL​)=263/35≈7.51. Power=263 W/7.51≈35 W (The option 32 W is the keyed answer, indicating the calculation method might differ slightly).",IOM
292,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Tube closed at one end containing air when excited produces the fundamental note of frequency 512 Hz. If the tube is open at both ends the fundamental frequency that can be excited is?,512 Hz,256 Hz,1024 Hz,768 Hz,C,"Calculation: Closed tube fundamental fc​=v/4L=512 Hz. Open tube fundamental fo​=v/2L. Since fo​=2fc​, fo​=2×512 Hz=1024 Hz.",IOM
293,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Tube closed at one end containing air when excited produces the fundamental note of frequency 512 Hz. If the tube is open at both ends the fundamental frequency that can be excited is?,512 Hz,256 Hz,1024 Hz,768 Hz,C,(Repeat of 285) 1024 Hz.,IOM
294,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,"The pendulum of clock is made of brass. Is the clock give correct time at 20 degree Celsius, how many seconds for day will it lose at 35 degree celsius?  (α brass=2×10−5 degree Celsius−1) ",13.5 sec,13 sec,12.96 sec,10 sec,C,Calculation: Δt=(1/2)αΔθ×T. Δt=(1/2)×(2×10−5)×(35−20)×(24×3600). Δt=10−5×15×86400=12.96 sec.,IOM
295,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,A body cools down from 65 degree Celsius to 60 degree celsius in 5 minutes. It will cool down 60 degree Celsius to 55 degree celsius in?,6 minutes,5 minutes,4 minutes,3 minutes,A,"Calculation (Newton's Law of Cooling): The average temperature (62.5∘C) in the first interval is higher than in the second (57.5∘C). The rate of cooling is proportional to the difference in temperature, so the second interval will take longer (i.e., >5 minutes).",IOM
296,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,"Acids, Bases & Salts",An object is placed at a distance 'u' from a simple microscope of focal length 'f'. The angular magnification obtained depends,Only on f,Only on u,On both u and f,None of the above,C,"Magnification M=1+D/f (final image at D) or M=D/f (final image at ∞). However, the object distance u is adjusted to get a clear image, so it ultimately depends On both u and f.",IOM
297,Physics,Electricity & Magnetism,Electric Circuits,A parallel bleach capacitor is charged and the charging battery is then disconnected. If the plates of the capacitor are moved for the apart by means of insulting handles:,Capacitance increases,Potential difference increases,Charge decreases,Potential difference decreases,B,"Since the battery is disconnected, Q remains constant. C∝1/d (decreases), and V=Q/C. Since C decreases, the Potential difference increases.",IOM
298,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,A thin stream of water from a tap is attracted by placing a rod near it. The rod is?,Charged rod,Uncharged rod,Metallic rod,Plastic rod,A,Attraction of a neutral stream of water indicates that the rod must be a Charged rod (electrostatic induction).,IOM
299,Physics,Mechanics,Motion & Forces,"The current in an electric bulb drops by 2%, the power decreases by? ",2%,4%,8%,10%,B,Calculation: P=I2R. The fractional change in power ΔP/P≈2×(ΔI/I). 2×2%=4%.,IOM
300,Chemistry,Mixed Topics,General Knowledge,Keratinized stratified squamous epithelium is found in?,Stomach,Intestine,Skin,Lungs,C,Keratinized stratified squamous epithelium forms the protective outer layer of the Skin.,IOM
